                "Presented by Art Fund" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/9c74c4c7-b45f-3f9d-8e2f-3d74555dc2b0> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Probably made by Mary, Queen of Scots, Elizabeth, Countess of Shrewsbury and members of her household at Sheffield Castle where Mary was imprisoned.\n\nOriginally all the panels were applied to a green velvet background, parts of which survive on the central panel and on several of the smaller panels.\n\nThe Oxburgh Hangings. Hanging with applied panels of embroidery, formerly at Oxburgh Hall, Norfolk."@en .

